WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.160
Compensation for 10,000 wolf-killed reindeer annually let Finnish herds grow and deplete winter

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:12.220
lichens. This is unintended consequences, episode 138. In the early 1990s, Finnish officials

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:17.720
began paying herders the full market value plus a 1.5 multiplier for every reindeer

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:23.180
carcass they could locate after a wolf kill. The payments were meant to end the cycle of retaliation

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.720
shootings that had driven wolves to the edge of extinction in the north. Instead, the same

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.520
Some rule removed any financial reason for herders to guard newborn calves.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.480
Rain deer numbers on the winter-likeened grounds climbed until the forage itself began to

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:36.900
disappear.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.180
Rain deer husbandry in Finland's northernmost districts had long operated under the shadow

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.360
of large carnivores.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:49.100
By the late 1980s, repeated wolf and bear attacks were pushing some cooperatives toward bankruptcy.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.240
Herders responded by shooting predators on site.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.340
Parliament therefore turned to a straightforward remedy already used in other Nordic countries.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.980
Direct monetary compensation for documented losses seemed the practical answer.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.040
The policy rested on two assumptions that seemed reasonable at the time.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:11.340
First, if the state reimbursed every verified kill, herders would stop killing wolves.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.600
Second, the payments would be modest because most carcasses would never be found in the vast

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.380
winter ranges.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:25.420
officials examined records showing that many herding districts lost calves during the snow-free months yet could rarely produce physical evidence.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:32.760
They therefore built a second computational payment stream based on district-level averages for calving success and predation rates.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:42.760
This two-part structure looked like a practical way to cover both visible and invisible losses without requiring herders to patrol every square kilometer of remote pasture.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:50.740
The compensation system was rolled out through the Reindeer Herder's Association Cooperatives and administered by the agency for rural affairs.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:59.660
Under the 2009 Game Animal Damages Act, a Herder received 1.5 times the current market value of any carcass that could be produced.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:05.060
A separate computational payment covered estimated calf losses between May and November.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.680
Districts that suffered repeated heavy losses qualified for a doubled multiplier.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.200
Earlier reports from the cooperatives noted a sharp drop in illegal wolf shootings.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:20.000
The Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry described the scheme as a successful model of coexistence.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:25.440
The European Union later imposed an annual ceiling of 10 million euros on total payouts.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:31.060
Because the calf-loss component relied on cooperative-wide estimates rather than individual counts,

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.180
payments flowed even when a particular herder chose not to increase fencing or night checks.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:41.320
The system therefore scaled quickly across the 20 northern most districts without requiring

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.900
new field staff or verification technology.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:49.100
Because compensation depended on locating a carcass, herders had little incentive to

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:52.980
invest time or money in calf protection once the payment rule was in place.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:58.380
Calf-loss models built into the system assumed average predation rates and paid cooperatives

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:01.740
regardless of whether individual herders had taken extra precautions.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:06.380
conditions. With the economic pressure to guard calves reduced, more animals survive

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:11.000
to winter pasture. Studies of the Finnish Norwegian border fence show that Leikin

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.000
biomass on the Finnish side, where year-round grazing is permitted, has fallen to roughly

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.780
one-third the level recorded on the Norwegian side that enforces strict seasonal rotation.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:27.060
The ambio-reconstruction of Leikin cover from 1959 onward attributes the decline primarily

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:32.300
to sustain trampling and foraging rather than simple consumption. As winter forage

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:37.700
thinned, reindeer ranged more widely in search of food. This increased encounters with wolves

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:42.500
that had begun to recolonize from the east. The same compensation payments that had lowered

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:48.480
direct persecution therefore contributed to larger reindeer populations, heavier pasture pressure

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.780
and renewed wolf presence. Districts qualifying for the doubled multiplier kept receiving

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:57.180
higher payments even as total Lycan cover continued to drop.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:02.920
This created a feedback loop in which poorer forage led to more visible losses and therefore

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:03.900
more compensation.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:09.480
The computational calf payments, calculated once every three years from district averages,

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.840
did not adjust downward when actual survival improved.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.380
So the financial signal to reduce herd size never appeared.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:23.040
By the mid-2010s, several cooperatives reported that Lycan pastures were producing visibly poorer

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.340
body condition and reindeer. The ministry began experimenting with supplemental feeding programs.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:33.120
The EU spending cap remained in force, so shortfalls and compensation were

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:38.860
pro-rated across claimants. No fundamental redesign of the per-head, ex-post-payment rule has

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:44.780
occurred. Herders continue to locate and report carcasses, yet the underlying dynamic of expanding

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:50.740
herds on shrinking forage persists. Recent vegetation inventories confirm that the contrast across

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:56.580
the Norwegian border fence has only widened since the compensation regime matured. Supplemental

00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:01.520
feeding has eased immediate weight loss for some animals, but has not restored like in biomass,

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.520
because the added feed does not reverse the trampling damage already done to the ground layer.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:11.040
When Finland tied compensation directly to the number of documented carcasses,

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:16.700
the rule rewarded the reporting of losses rather than the prevention of losses. This allowed calf

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:20.160
survival to rise without corresponding increases in herding effort.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:25.500
When the same rule was paired with computational calf payments calculated from district averages,

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.580
it further decoupled individual herder actions from financial outcomes.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:34.600
Total reindeer numbers were permitted to exceed the winter ranges long-term capacity.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.960
Decision makers who next designed predator compensation programs can test whether payments

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:44.640
are conditioned on verifiable protective measures before the first reindeer are counted.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:49.420
How might a similar payment rule behave if it were introduced today in another region

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:53.120
where large carnivores and domestic herds share shrinking forage?

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:54.660
That's the case for today.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.560
The lessons tend to travel further when you share them,

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:01.900
so send this one to someone who'd find it useful and subscribe wherever you're listening.

